course: dictionary
lesson: 13210
title: Furnished: three meanings in one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Furnished is a good example. Look at the words around it, because they are its clues.
explain: «We rented a furnished flat, so the beds and sofas were ready for us.» Beds and sofas are furniture, so furnished here means having furniture in it. Swap in your meaning: "a flat having furniture in it" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «The report furnished us with useful details.» Nothing is being put into a room here. Furnished means gave or supplied something we need. This is a formal use you will meet in stories and exam papers, and the words with and details are your clues.
fact: Furnished is an adjective when it describes a room or flat: a furnished flat has furniture in it.
fact: Furnish is a verb meaning to put furniture in a room. Its past form is furnished.
fact: «Fully furnished» means a place has everything needed inside; «sparsely furnished» means it has very little furniture.
fact: In formal writing, «furnished with» means supplied with something needed, such as details or information.
fact: A quick check: swap in "had furniture in it" or "supplied", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «We rented a furnished flat, so the beds and sofas were ready.» What does furnished mean? | Very large | Empty and cold | Painted in bright colours | *Having furniture in it
exercise: «Mum furnished the new bedroom with a desk and a bookcase.» What is Mum doing? | Painting the walls | Cleaning the windows | Closing the door | *Putting furniture in the room
exercise: «The report furnished us with useful details.» What does furnished mean here? | *Gave us what we needed | Had no furniture | Printed it in colour | Hid the details
test: «The hotel room was sparsely furnished, with only a bed.» What does sparsely furnished suggest? | Lots of furniture everywhere | Dirty and broken | *Very little furniture | Lit by candles
test: Ava says furnished means "fancy". Which is the best check? | Ask if it rhymes with fished | *Swap in "had furniture in it" and see if it still makes sense | Count the letters | Look only at the first word
exam: «The writer furnished the story with vivid details of the ancient castle.» What does furnished mean here? | Destroyed | Hidden | Decorated with furniture | *Supplied
